l, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15723, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019NadnY6VM2qGeXL4U6z1oK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18976, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_013xNeb52GZNcVDvLj38xdYg", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the fleet mixed; the retry completed the rollout. Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and should not be redeployed until it is investigated. Follow-up: investigate v2.3.1 failure, and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-2025-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 49576, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013xNeb52GZNcVDvLj38xdYg", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-2025-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 49576, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013xNeb52GZNcVDvLj38xdYg", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 52438, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0157vxxxTzijPBH5BcNbCDq3", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the fleet mixed; the retry completed the rollout. Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and should not be redeployed until it is investigated. Follow-up: investigate v2.3.1 failure, and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-2025-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 53038, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0157vxxxTzijPBH5BcNbCDq3", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-2025-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53038, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0157vxxxTzijPBH5BcNbCDq3", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 54980, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It reports healthy, and the error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging. Because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Rollback issues:** The first attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east, leaving the fleet mixed. The retry completed the rollout across all regions.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. The first request timed out, so I retried with the same idempotency key. The incident was created once.\n\nFollow-up needed:\n- Investigate why v2.3.1 fails health checks, and do not redeploy it until that is resolved.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01GT99XiU2Ua2neAEbZtVayB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0117zsYRyXderKarok1zYPF7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in all three regions. Rolling back to v2.3.0, which has already been healthy in production, so it doesn't need change-manager approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01YRKfwchPWzv49xe87x42HW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback returned a partial failure, with the rollout halted after us-east. I'll check the current state before doing anything else.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GM4syAvYnLS3cdXjPJMX2j", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout is now mixed: us-east is on v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. The target version is the same, so I'll retry the rollback once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Pmc3zWZxE8DzkyQLBeT1Ao", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019NadnY6VM2qGeXL4U6z1oK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "All three regions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy, with error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002. Next I'll open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013xNeb52GZNcVDvLj38xdYg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the fleet mixed; the retry completed the rollout. Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and should not be redeployed until it is investigated. Follow-up: investigate v2.3.1 failure, and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-2025-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. Since I set an idempotency key, a retry with the same key will run at most once, so I'll retry it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0157vxxxTzijPBH5BcNbCDq3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the fleet mixed; the retry completed the rollout. Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and should not be redeployed until it is investigated. Follow-up: investigate v2.3.1 failure, and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-2025-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It reports healthy, and the error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging. Because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Rollback issues:** The first attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east, leaving the fleet mixed. The retry completed the rollout across all regions.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001** for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. The first request timed out, so I retried with the same idempotency key. The incident was created once.\n\nFollow-up needed:\n- Investigate why v2.3.1 fails health checks, and do not redeploy it until that is resolved.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt.", "type": "text"}]}]}